 "text": "Hi, how have you been? I like your finger marks still wet still while the oil is still smelly. Varnishing too early ruining the oil. That's doable, but I'd varnish it in several thin coats rather than one thick one. You can varnish right after the oil is finished and buffed, and wait an hour before touching. It protects from dust while it dry. It' stop sticking to a cotton bud. You' never reoil it itself. If you think it still smells, leave it in a sealed box for week.",
